WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:11.610
30. Reusing versus recycling. Reusing and recycling may sound similar, but they are

2
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:17.670
actually quite different. Recycling has become more and more popular around the world in

3
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:24.990
the last 20 or 30 years, while people have reused materials throughout history. Nowadays,

4
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:30.770
people are talking more about reusing as a better alternative to recycling. So how is

5
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:37.970
reusing different from recycling? Well, reusing something means that the object is still used

6
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:44.850
for its original purpose. The goal of reusing is to help objects and materials lengthen their lives.

7
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:52.170
If you had an old oven, for example, you could reuse it by giving it to someone else. Maybe that

8
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:59.330
person could repair it or upgrade it, but still use it as an oven. Recycling it, on the other hand,

9
00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:06.330
means the oven is taken apart. Its parts are used in different ways in new objects. When you give

10
00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:12.570
away clothes for other people to wear, that is reusing them. Cutting clothes up into rags is

11
00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:21.330
recycling them. More people are now focusing on reusing in addition to recycling. They say reusing

12
00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:28.490
should be our first step before we think about recycling. Reusing uses less energy than recycling.

13
00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:35.690
It also causes less environmental damage because recycling often means that materials must be broken

14
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:42.890
down or melted in polluting factories. People also say reusing helps create communities and

15
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:50.490
helps people think about how they might be able to share more. Clearly, reusing and recycling will

16
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:56.990
both be important as we all try to be less wasteful. But perhaps recycling less should

17
00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:02.150
actually be our new goal, as long as it means we are all reusing more.
